Dan is the founder of ZipCPU, a project organized under his small business,
Gisselquist Technology. He is well known in the open source Electronic Design
Automation (EDA) community for his work, including the open source ZipCPU FPGA
core, as well as his many FPGA and Verilog tutorials and blog posts about FPGAs.

Dan publicly professes his Christian values and his company (and its projects)
are "Christian based".[[source]][0] His "values" were put on display when ZipCPU
was rejected for NLNet funding on the basis that Dan refused to agree to adopt
the IEEE Code of Ethics.[[source]][1] In his public statement on the matter, he
elaborates on these "values", revealing with pride his well-developed
transphobia, homophobia, and ableism, reserving the right to discriminate based
on "good moral character". Undocumented immigrants catch some strays as well in
his screed.

